      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>Main work of <t:persName role="author" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS14741GirgisY">Ǧirǧis al-Makīn ibn al-ʿAmīd (the Younger)</t:persName> containing an introduction on Christology, biblical exegesis,
               Coptic apologetics against Judaism, Islam, the Melkites and the Dyophysites as well as a refutation of astrology. It was translated into 
               Ethiopic by <t:persName role="translator" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8410Salikof">Salik</t:persName> towards 
               <t:date notBefore="1475" notAfter="1499">the end of the 15th century</t:date>. In the Ethiopic version it is attributed to a person 
               called "George, disciple of Anthony the Syrian". 
               According to the colophon of the work contained in some witnesses the text was translated from Greek into Arabic by <t:persName role="translator" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4374Gabreel">Gabrǝʾel Walda Batrak</t:persName>.
               Different dates of the translation are mentioned: <t:date calendar="hijri" when-custom="315" when="0928">315 year of the Hijrah, that is 928 CE</t:date> 
               in <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BNFet110">Paris, Bibliothèque nationale de France, BnF Éthiopien 110</t:ref> and <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BLorient778">London, British Library, BL Oriental 778</t:ref>; <t:date calendar="diocletian" when-custom="983" when="0991">983 year of martyrs, that is 991 CE</t:date> and 
               <t:date calendar="islamic" when-custom="665" when="1267">in the month <t:foreign xml:lang="ar">raǧab</t:foreign> in the year 665, that is 1267</t:date> in <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdd015">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy, Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi, C3-IV-241</t:ref>. 
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
